// Wisps (WorldActorHandler, Wisp, WispGlow): summoned with /dsactor as the warm-up starts, 16 blocks ahead, at night,
// over a walled sheet of water built high over plains, so no trees hide them (in a swamp the bench stood on a canopy
// and the leaves hid most of the lights) and no natural ones start: the scene's biome has none. Each wisp is one to four
// lights with their halos, motes and faint lights (the fireflies' light option, set on). A summoned one has a random
// number of lights and haunts, so compare with --spread. Two, as a marsh might show, and six, far more than ever start
// naturally. One lives a minute at least, and can live three, so the six have a sheet of their own, over savanna, or
// the next run's two would find them still there (the off runs clear them). Facing east, a little down. See README.md.
